From: Florian Fuchs <fuchsfl@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] serial: sh-sci: hold TxD at mark level while TE is off

Every termios change on the Dreamcast serial console (kernel console
open before "Run /init", mksh, top, ...) prints one garbage byte on the
host terminal.

sci_set_termios() calls sci_reset(), which writes SCSCR = 0 and so
clears TE.  On the SH7750 SCIF the TxD pin is then only driven when
SCSPTR.SPB2IO is set, with SPB2DT as the level.  The driver leaves
SPB2IO clear, so TxD floats for the duration of the reconfiguration and
the receiver sees a start bit followed by noise.

Set SPB2IO and SPB2DT before disabling TE so the line stays idle.  The
bits are ignored while TE=1, so normal transmission is unaffected.

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/sh-sci.c b/drivers/tty/serial/sh-sci.c
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/sh-sci.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/sh-sci.c
@@ -2647,6 +2647,16 @@
 	unsigned int status;
 	struct sci_port *s = to_sci_port(port);
 
+	/*
+	 * With TE=0 the TxD pin is only driven if SPB2IO is set, otherwise
+	 * it floats and the receiver on the other end sees a garbage byte
+	 * on every termios change.  Hold it at mark (idle) level instead.
+	 */
+	if (sci_getreg(port, SCSPTR)->size && s->regtype != SCIx_RZV2H_SCIF_REGTYPE) {
+		status = sci_serial_in(port, SCSPTR);
+		sci_serial_out(port, SCSPTR, status | SCSPTR_SPB2IO | SCSPTR_SPB2DT);
+	}
+
 	sci_serial_out(port, SCSCR, s->hscif_tot);	/* TE=0, RE=0, CKE1=0 */
 
 	reg = sci_getreg(port, SCFCR);
